          production: "MINING: 70% of silver is produced as a byproduct of base metal mining (copper, lead, zinc). Primary silver mines work epithermal vein deposits. Ore is crushed and floated to produce a silver-rich concentrate. PROCESSING: For polymetallic ores, silver is recovered during lead/copper smelting \u2014 it reports to the bullion phase. For dedicated silver ores, cyanide leaching (same as gold) or Merrill-Crowe process (zinc precipitation from cyanide solution) is used. REFINING: Silver dor\xE9 or silver-rich anode slimes from copper/lead refineries are refined by electrolysis (Moebius or Balbach process) to 99.9%+ purity.",
